prime-agent

Self-improving coding agent with IPython-backed kernel. Features
include LLM provider integration, conversation state persistence,
attachment handling, and a plugin/skill system.

This is the main coding-agent sub-package of the Prime Agent monorepo,
distributed as a pre-built npm package. The dist/ directory contains
compiled TypeScript output (ESM bundle).

Python skills and kernel runtime are provided by separate ports:
  - py-prime-agent-runtime (kernel-side runtime shim, rlm module)
  - py-prime-agent-skill-* (11 individual skill ports)
  - py-prime-agent-skills (meta-port installing all 11 skills)
  - py-prime-agent-science (meta-port installing scientific stack)

Node.js runtime dependencies:
  - prime-agent-core (agent engine)
  - prime-agent-ai (LLM provider abstraction)
  - prime-agent-tui (terminal UI)

The zeromq native addon is built against system libzmq4 via CMake
with ZMQ_SHARED=true.
